WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.740
In 1949, the philosopher Gilbert Ryle told
a story about a visitor to a university.

2
00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:11.640
He is shown the colleges, the libraries,
the sports fields, the offices.

3
00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:15.610
Then he asks: but where is the University?

4
00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.840
If scientists could map
every cell in your brain,

5
00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:21.380
would anything about you be left out?

6
00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:26.240
In this mission, you'll meet the views
that say the brain is the whole story.

7
00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:30.440
Then you'll meet Mary, a scientist
who knows every fact about colour,

8
00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:33.440
but has only ever seen black and white.

9
00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:38.090
Your mission: weigh up whether a full map
of your brain would leave anything about

10
00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:38.770
you out.
